# A WPF list box keeps keyboard focus on the LIST. The arrow keys move the
# SELECTION, and the item is announced through a selection event — there is no
# focus event per item at all.
#
# This produced total silence. Selection announcements had been given the focus
# validity predicate, so every one of them asked "is this item the focused
# element?", the answer was always no (the list is), and every announcement was
# swept as stale before it could be spoken.
#
# Staleness for a selection is a question about the selection. The "selection"
# cancel group already answers it: a newer one supersedes a pending older one.
# Asking an unrelated question on top of that could only ever subtract.

node list List "Settings categories" value=General
node c1   ListItem "General"  pos=1 size=7
node c2   ListItem "Speech"   pos=2 size=7
node c3   ListItem "Keyboard" pos=3 size=7

focus list
drain
select c1
drain
select c2
drain
select c3

expect
  Settings categories, list, General
  General, 1 of 7
  Speech, 2 of 7
  Keyboard, 3 of 7
